{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>יִכּוֹנֵנִי</b> — The meaning: I do not desire to do battle with the wicked, only if he strikes me — were he to strike me to chastise me, that which he is righteous — it would be kindness done to me, and he would rebuke me; this would be counted in my eyes like <b>oil of the head</b>. This is the opinion of R. Moses ha-Kohen. And according to my opinion: <b>oil of the head</b> is like בְּמַנְעֲמֵיהֶם (in their pleasant things). And the meaning: <b>oil of the head</b> like רֹאשׁ שֶׁמֶן, 'choicest oil' — they anoint with spices; <b>the head of the oil of the wicked</b> — let them not shatter my head, like וְלָמָּה תְנַיאוּן. And the proof: כִּי עוֹד וּתְפִלָּתִי בְּרָעוֹתֵיהֶם, for the nature of oil is to remove the breaking of the head; therefore this would be the opposite." "And he said: <b>יָנִיא</b> — corresponding to יִכּוֹנֵנִי." "And the meaning of <b>בְּרָעוֹתֵיהֶם</b> — that evil should come upon them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 141, :notes {0 "The lemma cited as יהלמני likely corresponds to יָכוֹכֵנִי in the verse; the translation preserves Ibn Ezra's spelling. The fragment ולמה תניאון is left untranslated as its relevance is cryptic; it may be a partial quotation or corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:39.509395740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}